* START-HISTORY:
* 24 Oct 26 dm  New.
* 28 Oct 26 dm  S.88 L2: the four boxes are panes of the layout service ($tk_layout): at 140 by 43 exactly the boxes the page has always drawn, in a bigger window the matrix shows more accounts and the
*               two lists under the cell more rows, every box wider, and the sentences about the cell are wrapped at the width of their box.  The resize key makes the layout again.
* 1 Nov 26 dm  A (all on) and N (all off) for the cursor's account, in the Gates menu too (owner: "buttons for All gates off and All Gates On"; warned once that all-on was
*              the one key this page never had, then: "just a convenience feature ... set all on, and then turn some off").  They QUEUE; R's box is still the question.  The
*              test of whether a cell can be queued is now one routine, cell.why, used by Enter, A and N.
* 1 Nov 26 dm  S.97 stage 2 (group B): the AI line ($tk_aipage), as tool.voc has it: F6 or AI > Ask the AI; the filter and refresh are offered to the model, nothing that changes a gate.
* 2 Nov 26 dm  S.88 p5-U2b P10: Ctrl-Q (and File > Quit, which the bar gives as Ctrl-Q) dropped every queued change without a word.  With anything queued it now asks first, in
*              $tk_confirm's box: Run the changes (each account's queue goes the way R takes it, its own box and, where a gate reaches beyond SD, the name typed; the page closes only
*              when nothing is left), Leave without them, or Cancel (the default: Enter alone never leaves).  With nothing queued it leaves at once, as before.  R's handler now
*              names the account (av) before run.queue, so that the leave question can run the queue of an account that is not under the cursor.
*              After the review: run.queue says whether its command ran without a refusal or an error (rq.ok); Run the changes keeps the page open and shows the
*              failing account's message when any did not succeed (run.queue clears a queue once the box said Run, so "nothing left" alone was not success).
* 7 Nov 26 dm  S.166: the home gate is a column (ON the home screen, off the command prompt; words start-menu and start-terminal).  A and N leave it alone: which of the two is
*              the tighter is not "off", so "all on" and "all off" do not decide where a person starts.
* 8 Nov 26 dm  S.176: F6 / Shift-F6 are the box keys of every page ($tk_aipage 'ring'): from the matrix to the AI line and back; AI > Ask the AI is a menu entry of its own.
*              Tab and Shift-Tab still move between the columns, the matrix's own use of them.
* 8 Nov 26 dm  S.179: Ctrl-T the theme (View > Theme) and Ctrl-K the keys of the page (Help > Keys), through $tk_std as on every page.
* 9 Nov 26 dm  S.186: View > Mouse and Ctrl-O (the log of the commands run), the same on every page (the cases act:std.mouse and ctrl-o, through $tk_std).
*              '/' finds an account on show by typing ($tk_findrow; the owner: "Letters stay, '/' finds").
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   TOOL.GATES
*
*   For the administrator only (it is refused, before anything is read, for anyone else; it is in SDSYS's VOC only).  A full-screen page, in the toolkit's frame (140 columns by
*   43 lines at least), with four boxes:
*
*     Gates by account      one row for each registered account (SDSYS is not one: modify.account refuses it), one column for each gate in $tk_gate_info's table, in the order
*                           modify.account carries them out: ON, off, - (the gate does not apply to this kind of account) or plan (not built yet).  A * after a cell is a change
*                           you have queued; the cell shows the state it would have.
*     The cell              what the gate under the cursor is: its two words, what ON allows, what OFF still allows, when a change reaches the person, whether it reaches
*                           beyond SD, and what it is as delivered
*     Who can reach ...     the accounts that have a gate on which reaches beyond SD
*     Sessions              the live sessions of the account under the cursor
*
*   Keys: arrows move over the cells, Enter or the space bar queues the opposite state for the cell (and again takes it back), R runs the queued changes of the account on the
*   cursor's row, U drops them, T queues OFF for every gate of that account that is off as delivered and on now (it does not touch a gate whose delivered state is on), F
*   changes which accounts are shown, F5 reads the machine again, F1 or ? or a click on a [?] explains the matrix, Ctrl-Q leaves (asking first when anything is queued: run the
*   changes, leave without them, or cancel, which is the default).  A (all on) and N (all off) queue every gate
*   of the cursor's account that can change to end ON or off (the owner's convenience, 1 Nov 2026: set all on, then turn some off); they only queue, as Enter does.
*
*   THE PAGE WRITES NOTHING ITSELF.  The queued changes of one account become ONE command, MODIFY.ACCOUNT name word word ..., which validates every word before it changes anything
*   (a conflict is refused whole), shown with its effect in a box answered Run or Cancel (Cancel is what Enter chooses) and run by $tk_run.  Turning ON a gate that reaches beyond
*   SD asks for the account's name to be typed, as every such step does; a gate that is off as delivered says so, and says that leaving it off is the tighter choice.  The route
*   gates ssh and api are one setting in modify.account (the words ssh, api, both and none SET it), so the page sends the one word that gives the pair of states you queued.
*   files-write needs files, and files-admin needs files-write: the page refuses a queue that breaks that before it asks, and the verb refuses it again.  After the command it reads
*   the machine again and shows the verb's own words; a cell is never changed on the page's say-so.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
program $tool_gates
$catalog $tool_gates

$include keys.h
$include int$keys.h
$include err.h
$include sl.h
$include tk.h

   prompt ''

   allow = 'modify.account'                                      ;* the one command this page may run

   call $tk_open('tool.gates', 'admin', ctx, err)
   if err # '' then
      display err
      stop
   end
   void kernel(K$AUDIT, 'tool start app=tool.gates')
   gosub declare.layout

   keys = ''
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f1', 'help', 'help', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'enter', 'queue', 'queue', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'r', 'run', 'run', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'u', 'drop', 'drop', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 't', 'tighten', 'tighten', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'a', 'all on', 'allon', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'n', 'all off', 'alloff', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f', 'filter', 'filter', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, '/', 'find', 'find', '', 1)                  ;* 9 Nov 26 (S.186): '/' finds an account by typing (letters are this page's commands)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f5', 'refresh', 'refresh', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'ctrl-q', 'quit', 'quit', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'esc', 'menu', 'menu', '', 1)                ;* S.88 U2: Esc takes the filter off first, else opens the menu bar
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'quit', '&File', '&Quit', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'queue', '&Gates', '&Queue the cell', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'run', '&Gates', '&Run the queue', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'drop', '&Gates', '&Drop the queue', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'tighten', '&Gates', '&Tighten the account', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'allon', '&Gates', '&All gates on', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'alloff', '&Gates', 'All gates o&ff', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'filter', '&View', '&Filter the accounts', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'find', '&View', 'Find an &account', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'refresh', '&View', '&Refresh', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'help', '&Help', '&Help on this page', '', '')
   call $tk_std('keys', ctx, keys, '', '')                ;* S.179: Ctrl-T theme, Ctrl-K keys and their View and Help entries, as on every page
   * S.97 stage 2 (group B): the AI line.  The page offers the AI only the filter and refresh (the gate matrix: queuing, tightening, dropping and running a change are NOT
   * offered without the owner's word); a proposal is carried out by the page's own key.  This page laid itself out first, so a line that took a row has the panes
   * declared again.
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'filter', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'refresh', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_aipage('init', ctx, keys, '', '', aout)
   if aout then gosub declare.layout

   CW = 6                                                        ;* width of a gate's cell (VIS, the account rows on the screen, and X0, the column of the first cell, come from the layout)
   fnames = 'all accounts' : @fm : 'accounts of persons' : @fm : 'accounts with a gate on that reaches beyond SD'

   ci = 1                                                        ;* the row under the cursor, among the rows shown
   gc = 1                                                        ;* the column under the cursor
   find.last = ''                                                ;* 9 Nov 26 (S.186): the text '/' asked for last
   ta = 0                                                        ;* the rows scrolled off the top
   flt = 0
   gen = 0
   msg = ''
   done = 0

   call $tk_gate_info('list', gids)
   NG = dcount(gids, @fm)
   gti = '' ; gon = '' ; goff = '' ; gwhen = '' ; gdef = '' ; gall = '' ; gstill = '' ; gbey = '' ; gstat = '' ; ghdr = ''
   for k = 1 to NG
      call $tk_gate_info(gids<k>, gi)
      gti<k> = gi<TK.G.TITLE>
      gon<k> = gi<TK.G.ON>
      goff<k> = gi<TK.G.OFF>
      gwhen<k> = gi<TK.G.WHEN>
      gdef<k> = gi<TK.G.DEFAULT>
      gall<k> = gi<TK.G.ALLOWS>
      gstill<k> = gi<TK.G.STILL>
      gbey<k> = gi<TK.G.BEYOND>
      gstat<k> = gi<TK.G.STATUS>
      gosub header.of
      ghdr<k> = hd
   next k

   an = 0
   anm = '' ; aty = '' ; asu = '' ; ast = '' ; aq = ''
   gosub read.all
   gosub draw.all

   loop
      call $tk_menubar('draw', ctx, keys, 'Gates', '', '', mr)              ;* the bar first: it writes row 0 whole, and the frame then writes the app name at its right end
      call $tk_frame(ctx, keys, 'Gates', msg)
      call $sl_curat(0, ctx<TK.C.YSTAT>)
      nm = ''
      screen key returning nm
      mr = ''
      ao = ''
      if nm # '' then call $tk_aipage('key', ctx, keys, 'Gates', nm, ao)             ;* S.97 stage 2: while the AI line has the focus it takes the keys, before the bar sees them
      if ao<1> = 'replay' then nm = ao<2>                                            ;* an action the AI proposed and the person accepted: this page's own key for it
      if ao<1> # '' then msg = ao<4>
      busy = (if flt # 0 then 1 else 0)
      if nm # '' and ao<1> = '' then call $tk_menubar('key', ctx, keys, 'Gates', nm, busy, mr)       ;* the Esc rule: a filter is taken off before the bar opens
      if mr<1> # '' then nm = mr<4>
      begin case
         case ao<1> = 'taken'
            if ao<3> then
               gen += 1                                                               ;* the preview, the wait and the answer covered the page: all of it is drawn again
               ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
               gosub draw.all
            end
         case nm = ''
            if status() = ER$EOF then exit
         case nm = 'guardquit'
            exit
         case nm = 'resize'
            call $tk_layout('refresh', ctx, '', lchg)
            gosub get.rects
            gosub keep.in.view
            gen += 1
            ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
            gosub draw.all
         case nm = 'mouse'
            gosub on.mouse
         case 1
            gosub on.key
      end case
      if done then exit
   repeat

   call $tk_close(ctx)
   stop

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- what the machine says

* The column heading of gate k: short, from the gate's id (a gate the page does not know by name is headed with the first five letters of its id)
header.of:
   gid = gids<k>
   begin case
      case gid = 'shared-read'
         hd = 'sh-rd'
      case gid = 'shared-write'
         hd = 'sh-wr'
      case gid = 'files-write'
         hd = 'f-wr'
      case gid = 'files-admin'
         hd = 'f-adm'
      case gid = 'sockets'
         hd = 'sock'
      case 1
         hd = gid[1, 5]
   end case
   return

* Every registered account but SDSYS, by name, each with its kind, its suspension and the state of every gate, read as $tk_gates reads them.  A queued change is kept
* by account name through a refresh, and is dropped for an account that has gone.
read.all:
   old.names = anm
   old.q = aq
   names = ''
   openpath @sdsys:@ds:'accounts' to acc.f then
      select acc.f to 9
      loop
         readnext id from 9 else exit
         if id # 'sdsys' then
            locate id in names<1> by 'AL' setting lp else
               ins id before names<lp>
            end
         end
      repeat
      close acc.f
   end
   an = 0
   anm = '' ; aty = '' ; asu = '' ; ast = '' ; aq = ''
   for i = 1 to dcount(names, @fm)
      call $tk_gates(names<i>, g, ainfo, gerr)
      if gerr = '' then
         an += 1
         anm<an> = names<i>
         aty<an> = ainfo<1>
         asu<an> = ainfo<2>
         for j = 1 to dcount(g, @fm)
            for k = 1 to NG
               if gids<k> = g<j, 1> then ast<an, k> = g<j, 2>
            next k
         next j
         locate anm<an> in old.names<1> setting op then
            for k = 1 to NG
               aq<an, k> = old.q<op, k>
            next k
         end
      end
   next i
   gosub make.view
   return

* The rows shown: the indexes of the accounts the filter lets through, in name order
make.view:
   view = ''
   nv = 0
   for i = 1 to an
      show = 1
      if flt = 1 and aty<i> # 'USER' then show = 0
      if flt = 2 then
         show = 0
         for k = 1 to NG
            if gbey<k> = 1 and gstat<k> = 'built' and ast<i, k> = 1 then show = 1
         next k
      end
      if show then
         nv += 1
         view<nv> = i
      end
   next i
   if ci > nv then ci = nv
   if ci < 1 then ci = 1
   if gc > NG then gc = NG
   if gc < 1 then gc = 1
   return

* The state account av will have once its queued changes are made: fin<k>, and the number of queued cells in qn
final.of:
   fin = ''
   qn = 0
   for k = 1 to NG
      if aq<av, k> # '' then
         fin<k> = aq<av, k>
         qn += 1
      end else
         fin<k> = ast<av, k>
      end
   next k
   return

* The queued cells of every other account than av
queued.elsewhere:
   qe = 0
   for i = 1 to an
      if i # av then
         for k = 1 to NG
            if aq<i, k> # '' then qe += 1
         next k
      end
   next i
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- drawing

* The layout (S.88 L2).  The four boxes are the panes of the layout service, declared in the sizes of the reference layout (140 by 43, the body 138 by 39): the matrix takes twice the rows
* the two lists under the cell take (the cell box stays as high as it is), and the two lists share the columns equally.  The page never hands the terminal over, so the declaration is
* made once, after the open, and the rectangles are fetched again after each 'refresh'.
* Out: mat (the matrix), cel (the cell), rea (who can reach the operating system), ses (the sessions), each .x .y .w .h; mtw, ctw, rtw, stw (the text width of each box); VIS (the
* account rows), CL (the lines about the cell), RW (the rows of each of the two lists), X0 (the column of the first cell).
declare.layout:
   ld = ''
   ld<1> = 'matrix' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 19 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 2 : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   ld<2> = 'cell' : @vm : 2 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 11 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   ld<3> = 'reach' : @vm : 3 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 9 : @vm : 68 : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   ld<4> = 'sessions' : @vm : 3 : @vm : 2 : @vm : 9 : @vm : 69 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   call $tk_layout('declare', ctx, ld, perr)
   if perr # '' then
      call $tk_close(ctx)
      display perr
      stop
   end
   gosub get.rects
   return

get.rects:
   call $tk_layout('pane', ctx, 'matrix', lrc)
   mat.x = lrc<1, 1> ; mat.y = lrc<1, 2> ; mat.w = lrc<1, 3> ; mat.h = lrc<1, 4>
   call $tk_layout('pane', ctx, 'cell', lrc)
   cel.x = lrc<1, 1> ; cel.y = lrc<1, 2> ; cel.w = lrc<1, 3> ; cel.h = lrc<1, 4>
   call $tk_layout('pane', ctx, 'reach', lrc)
   rea.x = lrc<1, 1> ; rea.y = lrc<1, 2> ; rea.w = lrc<1, 3> ; rea.h = lrc<1, 4>
   call $tk_layout('pane', ctx, 'sessions', lrc)
   ses.x = lrc<1, 1> ; ses.y = lrc<1, 2> ; ses.w = lrc<1, 3> ; ses.h = lrc<1, 4>
   mtw = mat.w - 4
   ctw = cel.w - 4
   rtw = rea.w - 4
   stw = ses.w - 4
   VIS = mat.h - 5                                               ;* the heading, the account rows, the two lines of counts and the border: 14 rows of 19
   CL = cel.h - 2                                                ;* the lines about the cell: 9 rows of 11
   RW = rea.h - 2                                                ;* the rows of each list under the cell: 7 of 9 (the last of them holds the "..." of the first list)
   X0 = mat.x + 28                                               ;* the column of the first cell (2 inside the box + the 26 of name and kind)
   return

* After a resize the rows scrolled off the top are not more than the accounts shown less the rows that fit
keep.in.view:
   if ta > nv - VIS then ta = nv - VIS
   if ta < 0 then ta = 0
   return

draw.all:
   cw2 = ctx<TK.C.W>
   chh = ctx<TK.C.H> - 5
   screen clear at 0,1 size cw2,chh
   screen box at mat.x,mat.y size mat.w,mat.h title 'Gates by account'
   screen box at cel.x,cel.y size cel.w,cel.h title 'The cell under the cursor'
   screen box at rea.x,rea.y size rea.w,rea.h title 'Who can reach the operating system'
   screen box at ses.x,ses.y size ses.w,ses.h title 'Sessions of the account under the cursor'
   gosub draw.matrix
   gosub draw.cell
   gosub draw.who
   gosub draw.sessions
   return

draw.matrix:
   s = fmt('Account', '20L') : fmt('Kind', '6L')
   for k = 1 to NG
      s := fmt(ghdr<k>, CW : 'L')
   next k
   screen text s at mat.x + 2,mat.y + 1 attr 'header' width mtw
   if ci <= ta then ta = ci - 1
   if ci > ta + VIS then ta = ci - VIS
   if ta < 0 then ta = 0
   for r = 1 to VIS
      kk = ta + r
      s = ''
      if kk <= nv then
         av = view<kk>
         s = fmt(anm<av>, '20L') : fmt(downcase(aty<av>), '6L')
         for k = 1 to NG
            gosub cell.text
            s := fmt(ct, CW : 'L')
         next k
         if asu<av> then s := ' susp'                    ;* S.166: seventeen cells leave five columns (the cell box below says "suspended" in full)
      end
      screen text s at mat.x + 2,mat.y + 1 + r attr (if kk = ci and kk <= nv then 'bold' else 'normal') width mtw
   next r
   if nv > 0 and ci <= nv then
      av = view<ci>
      k = gc
      gosub cell.text
      hx = X0 + (gc - 1) * CW
      hy = mat.y + 1 + ci - ta
      screen text fmt(ct, CW : 'L') at hx,hy attr 'highlight' width CW
   end
   if nv = 0 then screen text 'No account is shown.  F changes which accounts are shown.' at mat.x + 2,mat.y + 3 width mtw
   gosub draw.counts
   call $tk_help('mark', mat.x + mat.w - 5, mat.y + 1, 0, 0)
   return

* The text of the cell of account av, gate k: ON, off, a dash or plan, with a * when a change is queued
cell.text:
   s0 = ast<av, k>
   begin case
      case gstat<k> # 'built'
         ct = 'plan'
      case s0 = 'na'
         ct = '-'
      case 1
         d = (if aq<av, k> # '' then aq<av, k> else s0)
         ct = (if d = 1 then 'ON' else 'off') : (if aq<av, k> # '' then '*' else '')
   end case
   return

draw.counts:
   n.on = 0
   for i = 1 to an
      beyond.on = 0
      for k = 1 to NG
         if gbey<k> = 1 and gstat<k> = 'built' and ast<i, k> = 1 then beyond.on = 1
      next k
      n.on += beyond.on
   next i
   s = fnames<flt + 1> : ': ' : nv : ' of ' : an : ' account' : (if an = 1 then '' else 's') : '.  ' : n.on : ' with a gate on that reaches beyond SD.'
   screen text fmt(s, mtw : 'L') at mat.x + 2,mat.y + mat.h - 3 attr 'bold' width mtw
   if nv > 0 and ci <= nv then
      av = view<ci>
      gosub final.of
      gosub queued.elsewhere
      if qn > 0 then
         s = 'Queued for ' : anm<av> : ': ' : qn : ' change' : (if qn = 1 then '' else 's') : '.  R runs them as one command, U drops them.'
      end else
         s = 'Nothing queued for ' : anm<av> : '.'
      end
      if qe > 0 then s := '  Queued for other accounts: ' : qe : '.'
   end else
      s = ''
   end
   screen text fmt(s, mtw : 'L') at mat.x + 2,mat.y + mat.h - 2 width mtw
   return

* In plain sentences, for the cell under the cursor
draw.cell:
   lines = ''
   if nv > 0 and ci <= nv then
      av = view<ci>
      k = gc
      s0 = ast<av, k>
      lines<-1> = anm<av> : ' (' : downcase(aty<av>) : (if asu<av> then ', suspended' else '') : ')  -  ' : gti<k> : ' [' : gids<k> : ']'
      begin case
         case gstat<k> # 'built'
            lines<-1> = 'This gate is planned and not built yet: it has no words and nothing to switch.'
         case s0 = 'na'
            lines<-1> = 'This gate does not apply to a ' : downcase(aty<av>) : ' account: it is a route for a person, and the account has no Windows user of its own.'
         case (gids<k> = 'sh' or gids<k> = 'os') and aty<av> # 'USER'
            lines<-1> = 'Now: ' : (if s0 = 1 then 'ON' else 'off') : '.  A ' : downcase(aty<av>) : ' account is entered by whoever its Windows group admits, so a shell or OS.EXECUTE granted to it would be granted to all of them: modify.account refuses ' : gids<k> : ' for it, in either direction.'
         case 1
            lines<-1> = 'Now: ' : (if s0 = 1 then 'ON' else 'off') : '.  As delivered: ' : gdef<k> : '.  Words: ' : gon<k> : ' turns it on, ' : goff<k> : ' turns it off.' : (if aq<av, k> # '' then '  Queued: ' : (if aq<av, k> = 1 then 'ON' else 'off') : '.' else '')
            lines<-1> = 'ON allows: ' : gall<k>
            lines<-1> = 'OFF still allows: ' : gstill<k>
            lines<-1> = 'A change reaches the person: ' : gwhen<k> : '.  It does not touch a session that is already running.' : (if gbey<k> = 1 then '  This gate reaches BEYOND SD.' else '')
            if gids<k> = 'ssh' or gids<k> = 'api' then lines<-1> = 'ssh and api are ONE setting in modify.account (the words ssh, api, both and none set it): the page sends the one word that gives the pair you queue.'
            if gids<k> = 'files-write' then lines<-1> = 'files-write needs files; files-off takes it away too.'
            if gids<k> = 'files-admin' then lines<-1> = 'files-admin needs files-write; files-write-off and files-off take it away too.'
      end case
   end else
      lines<-1> = 'There is no account under the cursor.'
   end
   gosub wrap.lines
   for r = 1 to CL
      screen text fmt(lines<r>, ctw : 'L') at cel.x + 2,cel.y + r width ctw
   next r
   return

* A SCREEN TEXT longer than its width is cut, not wrapped
wrap.lines:
   wrapped = ''
   for wi = 1 to dcount(lines, @fm)
      if lines<wi> = '' then
         wrapped<-1> = ''
      end else
         call $tk_wrap(lines<wi>, ctw, pieces)
         wrapped<-1> = pieces
      end
   next wi
   lines = wrapped
   return

* Who can reach the operating system: the accounts with a gate on that reaches beyond SD, each with the gates
draw.who:
   n = 0
   for r = 1 to RW
      screen text space(rtw) at rea.x + 2,rea.y + r width rtw
   next r
   for i = 1 to an
      w = ''
      for k = 1 to NG
         if gbey<k> = 1 and gstat<k> = 'built' and ast<i, k> = 1 then w := (if w = '' then '' else ' ') : gids<k>
      next k
      if w # '' then
         n += 1
         if n < RW then screen text fmt(fmt(anm<i>, '18L') : w, rtw : 'L') at rea.x + 2,rea.y + n width rtw
         if n = RW then screen text fmt('...', rtw : 'L') at rea.x + 2,rea.y + RW width rtw
      end
   next i
   if n = 0 then screen text fmt('No account has a gate on that reaches beyond SD.', rtw : 'L') at rea.x + 2,rea.y + 1 width rtw
   return

draw.sessions:
   for r = 1 to RW
      screen text space(stw) at ses.x + 2,ses.y + r width stw
   next r
   if nv > 0 and ci <= nv then
      call !listu(udata)
      av = view<ci>
      n = 0
      for i = 1 to dcount(udata, @fm)
         v = udata<i>
         if v<1, 9> = anm<av> then
            n += 1
            if n < RW then screen text fmt('user ' : v<1, 1> : '  ' : v<1, 6> : '  ' : v<1, 7>, stw : 'L') at ses.x + 2,ses.y + n width stw
         end
      next i
      if n = 0 then screen text fmt('No session is in ' : anm<av> : ' now.', stw : 'L') at ses.x + 2,ses.y + 1 width stw
   end
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- keys and mouse

on.key:
   msg = ''
   if len(nm) = 1 and nm >= 'A' and nm <= 'Z' then nm = downcase(nm)
   begin case
      case nm = 'up'
         if ci > 1 then
            ci -= 1
            gosub redraw
         end
      case nm = 'down'
         if ci < nv then
            ci += 1
            gosub redraw
         end
      case nm = 'left' or nm = 'btab'
         if gc > 1 then
            gc -= 1
            gosub redraw
         end
      case nm = 'right' or nm = 'tab'
         if gc < NG then
            gc += 1
            gosub redraw
         end
      case nm = 'enter' or nm = ' '
         gosub queue.cell
      case nm = 'r'
         if nv > 0 then
            av = view<ci>
            gosub run.queue
         end
      case nm = 'u'
         gosub drop.queue
      case nm = 't'
         gosub tighten
      case nm = 'a'
         tv = 1
         gosub queue.all
      case nm = 'n'
         tv = 0
         gosub queue.all
      case nm = '/'                         ;* S.186: the next account on show whose name holds the text typed ($tk_findrow)
         fr.rows = ''
         for fr.r = 1 to nv
            fr.rows<fr.r> = anm<view<fr.r>>
         next fr.r
         call $tk_findrow(fr.rows, ci, find.last, fpos)
         if fpos < 0 then msg = sysmsg(15045, find.last)
         if fpos > 0 then ci = fpos
         gosub draw.all
      case nm = 'f'
         flt = mod(flt + 1, 3)
         ci = 1
         ta = 0
         gosub make.view
         gosub draw.all
         msg = 'showing ' : fnames<flt + 1>
      case nm = 'f1' or nm = '?'
         call $tk_help('box', 'tool.gates.matrix', hm, 0, 0)
         if hm # '' then msg = hm
      case nm = 'ctrl-t'                    ;* S.179: the theme, kept for the person - the same on every page ($tk_std)
         call $tk_std('theme', ctx, keys, '', std.r)
         if std.r<1> then gosub draw.all
         msg = std.r<2>
      case nm = 'act:std.mouse'             ;* S.186: View > Mouse, the same on every page ($tk_std)
         call $tk_std('mouse', ctx, keys, '', std.r)
         msg = std.r<2>
      case nm = 'ctrl-o'                    ;* S.186: the log of the commands this page ran (View > Output; $tk_std)
         call $tk_std('output', ctx, keys, '', std.r)
      case nm = 'ctrl-k'                    ;* S.179: the keys of this page, in a box
         call $tk_std('keylist', ctx, keys, 'Gates', std.r)
      case nm = 'f5'
         gosub read.all
         gosub draw.all
         msg = 'read the machine again'
      case nm = 'f6' or nm = 'shift-f6' or nm = 'act:ai'
         call $tk_aipage('ring', ctx, keys, 1, nm : @fm : 1, ap)            ;* S.176: F6 / Shift-F6 go round the boxes (one here: Tab keeps moving the columns) and the AI line
         msg = ap<2>
      case nm = 'ctrl-q'
         gosub leave.ask
      case nm = 'esc'
         if flt # 0 then
            flt = 0
            ci = 1
            ta = 0
            gosub make.view
            gosub draw.all
            msg = 'showing ' : fnames<flt + 1>
         end
   end case
   return

redraw:
   gosub draw.matrix
   gosub draw.cell
   gosub draw.sessions
   return

on.mouse:
   screen mouse returning mev else mev = ''
   if mev = '' then return
   mr = ''
   call $tk_menubar('click', ctx, keys, 'Gates', mev, '', mr)                     ;* a click on the bar on row 0
   if mr<1> # '' then
      nm = mr<4>
      if nm # '' then gosub on.key                          ;* a bar left with nothing chosen has no name: the status message stays
      return
   end
   call $tk_aipage('mouse', ctx, keys, 'Gates', mev, ap)                            ;* S.97 stage 2: a click on the AI line gives it the focus
   if ap # '' then
      msg = ap
      return
   end
   call $tk_help('hit', mev, mat.x + mat.w - 5, mat.y + 1, hit.m)
   if hit.m then
      call $tk_help('box', 'tool.gates.matrix', hm, 0, 0)
      if hm # '' then msg = hm
      return
   end
   if mev<1> = 'press' and mev<2> = 1 then
      mx = mev<3>
      my = mev<4>
      if my >= mat.y + 2 and my <= mat.y + 1 + VIS and mx >= mat.x + 2 and mx <= mat.x + mat.w - 3 then
         if ta + my - mat.y - 1 <= nv then
            ci = ta + my - mat.y - 1
            if mx >= X0 and mx < X0 + NG * CW then gc = int((mx - X0) / CW) + 1
            gosub redraw
         end
      end
   end
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- queueing and running

* Enter on a cell: queue the opposite of what the cell will be, or take a queued change back
queue.cell:
   if nv = 0 then return
   av = view<ci>
   k = gc
   s0 = ast<av, k>
   gosub cell.why
   if why # '' then
      msg = why
      return
   end
   d = (if aq<av, k> # '' then aq<av, k> else s0)
   nw = (if d = 1 then 0 else 1)
   aq<av, k> = (if nw = s0 then '' else nw)
   gosub redraw
   return

* Can gate k of account av be queued?  why is null when it can, else the reason (one test for Enter, A and N)
cell.why:
   why = ''
   begin case
      case gstat<k> # 'built'
         why = gti<k> : ' is planned and not built yet'
      case ast<av, k> = 'na'
         why = gti<k> : ' does not apply to a ' : downcase(aty<av>) : ' account'
      case (gids<k> = 'sh' or gids<k> = 'os') and aty<av> # 'USER'
         why = 'a ' : downcase(aty<av>) : ' account is entered by whoever its Windows group admits, so modify.account refuses ' : gids<k> : ' for it'
   end case
   return

* A (tv = 1) and N (tv = 0): every gate of the cursor's account that can be queued is queued to END in state tv; a gate already in it has its queue taken back.  The
* owner's convenience (1 Nov 2026: "any admin would set all on, and then turn some off"): nothing is changed here, R shows the one command in its box (a gate that reaches
* beyond SD still wants the account's name typed) and Enter on a cell takes a single gate back out first.
queue.all:
   if nv = 0 then return
   av = view<ci>
   n.q = 0
   for k = 1 to NG
      gosub cell.why
      if gids<k> = 'home' then why = 'where the account starts is not changed by all on or all off'     ;* S.166
      if why = '' then
         aq<av, k> = (if ast<av, k> = tv then '' else tv)
         if aq<av, k> # '' then n.q += 1
      end
   next k
   gosub redraw
   w.st = (if tv = 1 then 'ON' else 'OFF')
   msg = (if n.q = 0 then 'every gate of ' : anm<av> : ' that can change is ' : w.st : ' already' else 'queued ' : w.st : ' for ' : n.q : ' gate' : (if n.q = 1 then '' else 's') : ' of ' : anm<av> : '; Enter on a cell takes one back, R runs them')
   return

* U: drop the queue of the account on the cursor's row
drop.queue:
   if nv = 0 then return
   av = view<ci>
   gosub final.of
   if qn = 0 then
      msg = 'nothing is queued for ' : anm<av>
      return
   end
   dropped = qn                                                  ;* the redraw below counts the queue again (now empty)
   for k = 1 to NG
      aq<av, k> = ''
   next k
   gosub redraw
   msg = 'dropped the ' : dropped : ' queued change' : (if dropped = 1 then '' else 's') : ' of ' : anm<av>
   return

* T: queue OFF for every built gate that is off as delivered and on now, on the cursor's account.  A gate that is on as delivered is left alone.
tighten:
   if nv = 0 then return
   av = view<ci>
   n.q = 0
   for k = 1 to NG
      person.only = (gids<k> = 'sh' or gids<k> = 'os')
      if gstat<k> = 'built' and gdef<k> = 'off' and ast<av, k> = 1 and not(person.only and aty<av> # 'USER') then
         aq<av, k> = 0
         n.q += 1
      end
   next k
   gosub redraw
   msg = (if n.q = 0 then anm<av> : ' has no gate on that is off as delivered' else 'queued OFF for ' : n.q : ' gate' : (if n.q = 1 then '' else 's') : ' of ' : anm<av> : '; R runs them')
   return

* R: the queued changes of account av (R's handler gives the cursor's row; run.all gives each account in turn), as one MODIFY.ACCOUNT command, its effect, Run or Cancel, then the
* machine's answer
run.queue:
   rq.ok = 0                                                     ;* 2 Nov 26 (review): 1 only when the box said Run and the command ran without a refusal or an error
   rq.ran = 0
   gosub final.of
   if qn = 0 then
      msg = 'nothing is queued for ' : anm<av>
      return
   end
   gosub check.needs
   if bad # '' then
      msg = bad
      return
   end
   gosub make.sentence
   call $tk_confirm(sent, el, typed, res, cmsg)
   if res = 'run' then
      call $tk_run(allow, sent, out, stat, err)
      rq.ran = 1
      rq.ok = (err = '' and stat >= 0)                           ;* modify.account's failures are negative codes ($tk_run: the command's @system.return.code)
      if err # '' then
         msg = err
      end else
         said = ''                                               ;* the verb's last line: for several words it is the closing line (which were carried out)
         for oi = dcount(out, @fm) to 1 step -1
            if trim(out<oi>) # '' then
               said = trim(out<oi>)
               exit
            end
         next oi
         msg = (if said # '' then said[1, 130] else 'ran, status ' : stat)
      end
      for k = 1 to NG
         aq<av, k> = ''
      next k
      gosub read.all
      gosub draw.all
   end else
      msg = cmsg
   end
   return

* files-write needs files, and files-admin needs files-write: refuse a queue that breaks it, before asking (the verb refuses it again)
check.needs:
   bad = ''
   fi = 0 ; fw = 0 ; fa = 0
   for k = 1 to NG
      if gids<k> = 'files' then fi = k
      if gids<k> = 'files-write' then fw = k
      if gids<k> = 'files-admin' then fa = k
   next k
   if fw > 0 and fi > 0 then
      if fin<fw> = 1 and fin<fi> # 1 then bad = 'files-write needs files: queue files ON as well, or files-write OFF'
   end
   if fa > 0 and fw > 0 then
      if fin<fa> = 1 and fin<fw> # 1 then bad = 'files-admin needs files-write: queue files-write ON as well, or files-admin OFF'
   end
   return

* The sentence for account av from its queued cells (fin holds the states it will have), and its effect for the box
make.sentence:
   words = ''
   rs = 0 ; ra = 0
   for k = 1 to NG
      if gids<k> = 'ssh' then rs = k
      if gids<k> = 'api' then ra = k
   next k
   route.changed = 0
   if rs > 0 then
      if aq<av, rs> # '' then route.changed = 1
   end
   if ra > 0 then
      if aq<av, ra> # '' then route.changed = 1
   end
   for k = 1 to NG
      if aq<av, k> # '' and k # rs and k # ra then
         words<-1> = (if aq<av, k> = 1 then gon<k> else goff<k>)
      end
   next k
   rword = ''                                                    ;* NOT rw: names are case-insensitive and RW is the rows of each list (get.rects); rw overwrote it and the page stopped in draw.who
   if route.changed then
      begin case
         case fin<rs> = 1 and fin<ra> = 1
            rword = 'both'
         case fin<rs> = 1
            rword = 'ssh'
         case fin<ra> = 1
            rword = 'api'
         case 1
            rword = 'none'
      end case
      words<-1> = rword
   end
   sent = 'modify.account ' : anm<av> : ' ' : trim(change(words, @fm, ' '))
   el = ''
   typed = ''
   loosen = 0
   beyond = 0
   whens = ''
   for k = 1 to NG
      if aq<av, k> # '' then
         if aq<av, k> = 1 then
            el<-1> = 'ON  - ' : gti<k> : ': ' : gall<k>
            if gdef<k> = 'off' then loosen = 1
            if gbey<k> = 1 then beyond = 1
         end else
            el<-1> = 'off - ' : gti<k> : ': it will still be able to ' : gstill<k>
         end
         locate gwhen<k> in whens<1> setting wp else whens<-1> = gwhen<k>
      end
   next k
   if route.changed then el<-1> = 'ssh and api are one setting: the word sent is ' : rword : ', which gives ssh ' : (if fin<rs> = 1 then 'ON' else 'off') : ' and api ' : (if fin<ra> = 1 then 'ON' else 'off') : '.'
   if loosen then
      el<-1> = 'A gate that is off as delivered is being turned ON.  Leaving it off is the tighter choice; you decide.'
   end
   if beyond then
      el<-1> = 'A gate that reaches beyond SD is being turned ON, so the account name has to be typed.'
      typed = anm<av>
   end
   el<-1> = 'A running session is not changed.  A change reaches the person: ' : change(whens, @fm, '; ') : '.'
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- leaving

* Ctrl-Q, and File > Quit (the bar gives its quit entry as ctrl-q): the page leaves at once when no account has anything queued.  When one has, $tk_confirm asks first (S.88 p5-U2b
* P10, 2 Nov 26; until then the queue was dropped without a word): Run the changes, Leave without them, or Cancel, which is the last button and so the default (Enter alone never
* leaves and never runs).  The box shows the command each account's queue would be; nothing is run here: Run the changes is run.all, which is R for each account in turn.
leave.ask:
   lq.sent = ''
   lq.n = 0
   lq.cells = 0
   for av = 1 to an
      gosub final.of
      if qn > 0 then
         lq.n += 1
         lq.cells += qn
         gosub make.sentence
         lq.sent<-1> = sent
      end
   next av
   if lq.n = 0 then
      done = 1
      return
   end
   lq.lines = lq.cells : ' queued change' : (if lq.cells = 1 then '' else 's') : ' of ' : lq.n : ' account' : (if lq.n = 1 then '' else 's') : ' not run yet.  Leaving the page drops them.'
   lq.lines<-1> = 'Run the changes shows the box R shows for each account in turn (its command, and its name to type where a gate reaches beyond SD); the page closes only when nothing is left.'
   lq.lines<-1> = 'Leave without them closes the page and changes nothing.  Cancel goes back to the page.'
   call $tk_confirm(change(lq.sent, @fm, '; '), lq.lines, '', lq.res, lq.msg, 'Leave the gate matrix?', '&Run the changes,&Leave without them,&Cancel')
   begin case
      case lq.res = 'alt'
         done = 1
      case lq.res = 'run'
         gosub run.all
      case 1
         msg = 'nothing was run; the queued changes are still here'
   end case
   return

* Run the changes: each account with a queue goes through run.queue once (its own box; a Cancel or a refusal there leaves its queue), found again by name after every command,
* since run.queue reads the machine again.  The page leaves only when no queue is left.
run.all:
   lq.tried = ''
   lq.fail = 0 ; lq.failmsg = ''                                 ;* 2 Nov 26 (review): a refused or failed command keeps the page open and its message is shown
   loop
      lq.av = 0
      for lq.i = 1 to an
         if lq.av = 0 then
            locate anm<lq.i> in lq.tried<1> setting lq.p else
               av = lq.i
               gosub final.of
               if qn > 0 then lq.av = lq.i
            end
         end
      next lq.i
   while lq.av > 0 do
      av = lq.av
      lq.tried<-1> = anm<av>
      gosub run.queue
      if rq.ran and not(rq.ok) then
         lq.fail += 1
         lq.failmsg = anm<av> : ': ' : msg
      end
   repeat
   lq.left = 0
   for av = 1 to an
      gosub final.of
      lq.left += qn
   next av
   begin case
      case lq.fail > 0
         msg = lq.fail : ' command' : (if lq.fail = 1 then '' else 's') : ' did not succeed, so the page stays: ' : lq.failmsg
      case lq.left = 0
         done = 1
      case 1
         msg = lq.left : ' queued change' : (if lq.left = 1 then '' else 's') : ' not run, so the page stays: ' : msg
   end case
   return

end

